INTERPRETATION
The proof program expands the ordinary stable five-step kernel margin in
six exhaustive nonnegative-coordinate chambers.  It separately expands
the nearest affine wall k=2q+2 in fourteen exhaustive chambers for Q>=7
and checks all 54 values with 1<=Q<=6.  Every emitted rational coefficient
is nonnegative.  These coefficient checks are unbounded in the chamber
variables.  The analyzer independently evaluates finite fusion recurrence
values through level 300 and verifies 1,130,350 evaluations of the
three-image Kac-Walton formula against that recurrence.  Its scan is a
bounded formula audit, not the proof of intermediate affine-wall distances.

